---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Update protocol"
  description="How /thinkos-update fetches the latest, detects drift on managed files, and re-applies without touching your vault."
  current="update-protocol"
>
  <p>
    <code>/thinkos-update</code> keeps Think OS current without a re-install.
    It fetches the latest commits from the upstream repo, summarizes what
    changed, checks managed files for local drift, and re-applies the curated
    instructions and slash commands atomically. Your vault is never touched.
  </p>

  <h2>What it updates</h2>
  <p>
    Think OS tracks two categories of files in
    <code>~/.thinkos/install-manifest.json</code>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Managed files</strong> — curated instructions and slash command
      playbooks that ship with the repo and are expected to evolve. The update
      command owns these.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your content</strong> — vault markdown, state files, and anything
      you've edited. These are never touched by an update.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Drift detection</h2>
  <p>
    Before overwriting any managed file, the command compares the on-disk sha256
    against the hash recorded at install time. If they differ — meaning you edited
    the file locally — it shows you the diff and asks before proceeding. You can
    keep your local version, take the upstream version, or merge manually.
  </p>

  <h2>Manifest v2</h2>
  <p>
    The install manifest now carries <code>managed_files</code> (array of paths
    with install-time hashes), <code>thinkos_version</code>, <code>channel</code>,
    <code>repo_path</code>, and <code>last_updated_at</code>. If your manifest
    is v1, run:
  </p>
  <pre class="bg-soft border border-rule rounded px-5 py-4 font-mono text-[14px] overflow-x-auto">bash scripts/thinkos-migrate-manifest-v1-to-v2.sh</pre>

  <h2>Running an update</h2>
  <p>
    From any Claude Code session:
  </p>
  <pre class="bg-soft border border-rule rounded px-5 py-4 font-mono text-[14px] overflow-x-auto">/thinkos-update</pre>
  <p>
    For a non-interactive terminal refresh:
  </p>
  <pre class="bg-soft border border-rule rounded px-5 py-4 font-mono text-[14px] overflow-x-auto">cd ~/code/think-os
bash scripts/thinkos-update.sh --pull</pre>

  <h2>Doctor checks</h2>
  <p>
    Four new <code>install:*</code> checks were added to
    <code>scripts/thinkos-doctor.sh</code>: <code>install:manifest-version</code>,
    <code>install:version</code>, <code>install:updates</code>, and
    <code>install:drift</code>. Run <code>bash scripts/thinkos-doctor.sh --deep</code>
    to see update and drift status at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Full protocol</h2>
  <p>
    For the complete design — file categories, atomic swap behavior, backup and
    restore — see
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os-personal/blob/main/docs/update-protocol.md">
      docs/update-protocol.md
    </a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
